   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ADB201 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.3</span>\n<h2>The 6 course learning outcomes (CLO), verbatim</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Exam questions are written against these outcomes — use them as your checklist.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13669 · Decision 1318/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 27/11/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ADB201 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.3</span>\n<h2>6 chuẩn đầu ra môn học (CLO), nguyên văn</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Đề thi được ra theo các chuẩn đầu ra này — dùng chúng làm danh sách tự kiểm.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13669 · QĐ 1318/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 27/11/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>CLO</th><th>Details (verbatim)<br><small>Nội dung (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>CLO1</strong></td><td>Apply the Fundamentals of book design: Understand the essential elements of book anatomy and design principles for effective layouts. Select appropriate typefaces, visual elements to effectively communicate content and engage different audiences.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>CLO2</strong></td><td>Master Manual bookbinding techniques and Creative material use: Demonstrate proficiency in basic bookbinding methods (folding, stitching, gluing). Experiment with materials and techniques to achieve unique visual and tactile effects.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>CLO3</strong></td><td>Explore Art book design concepts and Ideation: Analyze diverse examples of art books and their unique approaches. Develope creative concepts for book projects, considering form, content and audience engagement.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>CLO4</strong></td><td>Conduct Design research and Project execution: Formulate research questions to guid the book design process. Design and execute the book project, demonstrating conceptual thinking and technical skills.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>CLO5</strong></td><td>Evaluate Design solutions and Adapt to context: Critically assess book designs, considering their suitability for cultural and technical contexts. Select and justify the use of manual and/or digital methods to achieve specific design goals.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>CLO6</strong></td><td>Develop Professionalism and Collaborative skills: Exhibit a dedicated work ethic, attention to detail, and a willingness to experiment and refine designs. Contribute effectively to team projects and the ability to give and receive constructive feedback.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13669\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13669</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13669\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13669</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
